# Always push after changes

When you make changes to this project, always commit and push to GitHub at the end of each task or user request — without waiting to be asked.

- Commit only when there are actual changes to push
- Do not push secrets or credential files
- Use the existing commit message style (concise, why-focused)
- Confirm the push succeeded before finishing your response
